   <taskbody>
      <context>
         <p>During the process of commissioning an SMS device, the SMS mobile app provides an option to save the network information. The network details are saved on the Network profiles page.</p>
         <p>You can update or delete your network profile information at any time.</p>
         <p>To manage a network profile:</p>
      </context>
      <steps id="steps_103141170">
         <step>
            <cmd>On the SMS mobile app, tap Settings on the bottom menu.</cmd>
            <info>
               <p>The <b>Settings</b> page is displayed.</p>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Tap Network Profiles.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>placeholder</title>
                  <image height="501" href="../media/image120.png" placement="break" width="257">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
               <p>Figure  Settings - Network Profiles option</p>
               <p>The saved network profile is displayed.</p>
               <fig>
                  <title>placeholder</title>
                  <image height="501" href="../media/image121.png" placement="break" width="251">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
               <p>Figure  Network profiles page</p>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Tap the network name to view its details.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>placeholder</title>
                  <image height="501" href="../media/image122.png" placement="break" width="251">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
               <p>Figure  Network details page</p>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Select or update the security type and password and tap SAVE.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>To delete a network profile, tap DELETE.</cmd>
            <info>
               <p>A confirmation message is displayed.</p>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Tap DELETE.</cmd>
         </step>
      </steps>
   </taskbody>
</task>
